{"author":"Joe Oakhart","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"content_hash":"6192bf8302a20700d883f8e27bea46437d6551e0edf9af2f3e111980a50fd0aa","digest":{"component_or_area":"application-wide operation-scoped configuration and provider authentication composition","key_entities":["OperationSnapshot","RP-01","RP-04","ADR 0098","PydanticAIRunner","ProviderSession","GitRuntime","LLMRuntime","BridgeRuntime","op-cert","REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH","REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY","REBAR_OPERATION_SNAPSHOT_SHADOW","REBAR_ROOT","check_config_reads.py","SecretStr","SecretBytes","Langfuse","OTLP","resolve_with_sources","bridge check-access","bridge status","bridge fsck","review-plan"],"problem_keywords":["configuration resolution","authentication composition","credential handling","operation scoping","provider auth","environment isolation","ambient state","mid-operation behavior change"],"propositions":["Configuration resolution must follow a stable, immutable precedence order (explicit operation input > environment > project config > user config > schema default) with no mid-operation rereading of ambient state, files, cwd, or global config.","Authentication must be composed consistently across LLM, Git, bridge, MCP, review-bot, op-cert, and observability boundaries using provider-native bindings without a universal credential store or automatic keyring fallback.","Static credentials must be handled only through provider-specific non-serializable Pydantic carriers (SecretStr/SecretBytes) revealed only in sending adapters and never persisted in serialization, logs, exceptions, or subprocess arguments.","Op-cert must validate and copy the operation certificate key into a process-owned 0700 directory with 0600 file permissions at startup from exactly one of REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH or REBAR_OPCERT_PRIVATE_KEY, with no per-job retrieval or SSM/boto3 runtime coupling.","Same-capability children must inherit the ambient environment, owning children must receive only their adapter overlay, and unrelated sibling children must have exact Rebar-declared secret names removed with no global os.environ mutation.","An AST ownership gate must derive config and credential names from authoritative registries, reject direct/aliased config reads and backend reloads below approved seams, and maintain zero legacy exceptions at cutover."]},"digest_hash_version":1,"model":"bedrock:us.anthropic.claude-opus-4-8","schema":"ticket_digest_v1"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"TICKET_DIGEST","timestamp":1787541815573783001,"uuid":"f062687d-6f9b-4a27-b218-4a82e55435e6"}